  "worked_solution": "At the point where $t=0$,  the vector ${r}^{\u2032}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{\u2032}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =\u27e80,\\,{e}^{0},\\,{e}^{-0}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,1,\\,1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{\u2032}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{-t}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(0) & =\u27e81,\\,{e}^{0},\\,-{e}^{-0}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,1,\\,-1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point \n where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=\u27e80,\\,1,\\,1\u27e9+u\u27e81,\\,1,\\,-1\u27e9,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
